WEBVTT

00:00:04.060 --> 00:00:04.160
One
One!

00:00:04.160 --> 00:00:04.720
One!

00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:14.440
Outside of the window...

00:00:14.440 --> 00:00:19.500
I look up towards the blue sky...

00:00:26.050 --> 00:00:28.320
Yunocchi should be back soon.

00:00:35.230 --> 00:00:36.780
Wasshoi! Washoshoi!

00:00:37.030 --> 00:00:39.630
Question, question, question,
question, question mark

00:00:39.630 --> 00:00:43.000
Lazing, lazing, lazing, lazing, lazing about

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:44.940
What should we do?

00:00:44.940 --> 00:00:50.110
For now, let's just yell "Wasshoi!"

00:00:50.110 --> 00:00:51.640
Wasshoi! Washoshoi!

00:00:51.640 --> 00:00:53.040
Wa! Shoi!

00:00:55.250 --> 00:00:56.710
Wasshoi! Washoshoi!

00:00:59.120 --> 00:01:01.720
Even an absurd response

00:01:01.720 --> 00:01:04.620
Is sensible for someone from Jupiter

00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:06.730
Launch a rocket at random

00:01:06.730 --> 00:01:09.560
And approach the place where it lands

00:01:09.560 --> 00:01:14.230
After a pleasant nap

00:01:14.600 --> 00:01:18.640
Sure enough, sure enough,
my eyes tear when I yawn

00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:19.800
Good morning

00:01:19.800 --> 00:01:20.970
Let's play!

00:01:20.970 --> 00:01:23.680
Let's have a serious bread-eating race

00:01:23.680 --> 00:01:24.810
Wasshoi! Washoshoi!

00:01:24.810 --> 00:01:27.350
Who, who, who, who, who is it?

00:01:27.350 --> 00:01:30.680
Hungry, hungry, hungry,
hungry, hungry person

00:01:30.680 --> 00:01:35.090
Girls live off snacks

00:01:35.090 --> 00:01:36.860
Wasshoi! Washoshoi!
Rolling, rolling, rolling, golfing around

00:01:36.860 --> 00:01:37.660
Rolling, rolling, rolling, golfing around

00:01:37.660 --> 00:01:40.990
Lazing, lazing, lazing, lazing, lazing about

00:01:40.990 --> 00:01:44.900
Let's look up at the sun

00:01:44.900 --> 00:01:48.170
Wasshoi! Wasshoi!

00:01:48.170 --> 00:01:50.700
In a dream, in a dream with everyone
Wasshoi! Wasshoi!

00:01:50.700 --> 00:01:53.270
I had the same conversation

00:01:53.270 --> 00:01:57.180
Question mark and wasshoi 365

00:01:57.180 --> 00:01:58.970
Wasshoi! Washoshoi!

00:02:00.080 --> 00:02:04.550
January 10 Welcome Back... Ms. Ume

00:02:15.660 --> 00:02:16.890
I'm back.

00:02:17.530 --> 00:02:19.730
It really feels good to go home.

00:02:19.730 --> 00:02:22.390
This place really is home to me as well.

00:02:23.030 --> 00:02:24.870
There's a familiar nameplate.

00:02:25.870 --> 00:02:28.670
I wonder if the Christmas tree is still up?

00:02:29.570 --> 00:02:31.370
It's being reused?

00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:36.100
Wow, there's a lot.

00:02:38.020 --> 00:02:39.650
Welcome back, Yuno.

00:02:39.650 --> 00:02:41.710
I'm back, Miya-chan.

00:02:42.720 --> 00:02:45.060
Happy New Year, I hope to see you around.

00:02:45.060 --> 00:02:46.420
How did it feel to go back home?

00:02:47.160 --> 00:02:49.990
I was really happy to see my parents
for the first time in a while.

00:02:49.990 --> 00:02:51.300
That's good.

00:02:51.300 --> 00:02:54.230
Everyone told me I got bigger.

00:02:57.570 --> 00:02:59.440
Let's go in, it's cold.

00:02:59.440 --> 00:03:01.130
I wonder if it's cold indoors too?

00:03:04.180 --> 00:03:07.010
Sorry, this isn't much different
from outside, is it?

00:03:07.010 --> 00:03:08.350
It's all right.

00:03:08.350 --> 00:03:10.780
I don't turn on the heater during the daytime.

00:03:10.780 --> 00:03:12.780
What a rugged lifestyle.

00:03:12.780 --> 00:03:16.380
I was fine at home, but it's colder here.

00:03:16.890 --> 00:03:18.020
Here you go.

00:03:18.020 --> 00:03:19.320
Thank you.

00:03:19.320 --> 00:03:21.260
When did you get back, Miya-chan?

00:03:21.330 --> 00:03:26.300
Early this morning, Sae and Hiro are back too.

00:03:26.300 --> 00:03:28.660
I was the last one.

00:03:31.970 --> 00:03:34.460
I can feel it warming me up from the inside!

00:03:34.840 --> 00:03:35.940
Did that warm you up?

00:03:35.940 --> 00:03:37.880
Seconds!

00:03:37.880 --> 00:03:39.640
Happy New Year!

00:03:39.640 --> 00:03:41.750
I got lots of New Year's cards!

00:03:41.750 --> 00:03:43.180
Oh, here's one from Yamaguchi.

00:03:43.180 --> 00:03:44.720
Oh, there's even one from Kiyomi.

00:03:44.720 --> 00:03:46.280
I got some too.

00:03:46.280 --> 00:03:49.690
It's a lot of trouble to write them,
but it sure feels good to receive them.

00:03:49.690 --> 00:03:50.620
Yeah...

00:03:50.620 --> 00:03:53.820
I only write back to the people
who send me cards though.

00:03:53.820 --> 00:03:54.930
Really?

00:03:54.930 --> 00:03:58.130
Say, Yunocchi, did you bring
anything from home?

00:03:58.130 --> 00:04:02.030
Yeah, I brought mochi, and other things,
like tsukudani.

00:04:02.030 --> 00:04:03.430
I did too.

00:04:03.430 --> 00:04:06.630
It was all food, so my bag
was incredibly heavy.

00:04:08.270 --> 00:04:10.910
I've got to visit Hiro and Sae later.

00:04:10.910 --> 00:04:12.140
I have souvenirs for them.

00:04:12.140 --> 00:04:13.770
I'll go too!

00:04:14.480 --> 00:04:15.970
Then, let's go together.

00:04:16.380 --> 00:04:17.370
All right!

00:04:19.980 --> 00:04:21.020
Sae!

00:04:21.020 --> 00:04:21.320
Snooze...
Sae!

00:04:21.320 --> 00:04:23.480
Snooze...

00:04:26.460 --> 00:04:27.260
Hiro!

00:04:27.260 --> 00:04:27.690
Snooze...
Hiro!

00:04:27.690 --> 00:04:30.030
Snooze...
Miya-chan, what time is it right now?

00:04:30.030 --> 00:04:31.720
Snooze...
I think it's about 2 PM.

00:04:32.130 --> 00:04:34.220
Happy New Year.

00:04:37.030 --> 00:04:42.040
U-Umm, good mor... I mean,
Happy New Year.

00:04:42.040 --> 00:04:43.970
Sorry for waking you up.

00:04:43.970 --> 00:04:46.980
Happy New Year, Hiro.

00:04:46.980 --> 00:04:49.880
Happy New Year, Sae.

00:04:49.880 --> 00:04:51.970
I hope to see you around this year.

00:04:52.080 --> 00:04:53.310
Happy New Year.

00:04:54.190 --> 00:04:57.620
Going back home really
disrupts my daily rhythm.

00:04:57.860 --> 00:05:00.690
You end up letting others do
all the household chores.

00:05:00.690 --> 00:05:01.760
When did you get back?

00:05:01.760 --> 00:05:06.230
I came back yesterday,
about the same time as Hiro.

00:05:06.230 --> 00:05:07.330
Yeah...

00:05:07.330 --> 00:05:09.230
You two took your time.

00:05:09.230 --> 00:05:12.000
Yeah, we let ourselves go.

00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:14.640
I let myself go too much.

00:05:14.640 --> 00:05:20.010
I ate food, went into the kotatsu and
chatted while watching the TV.

00:05:21.180 --> 00:05:23.180
Now's not the time to be sleeping.

00:05:23.180 --> 00:05:25.020
I've got to walk to burn off calories.

00:05:25.020 --> 00:05:27.040
Then, let's take a walk together.

00:05:27.350 --> 00:05:28.920
Let's make our first shrine visit of the year.

00:05:28.920 --> 00:05:32.420
I want to go too. I want to buy milk.

00:05:32.420 --> 00:05:33.590
The first shrine visit of the year?

00:05:33.590 --> 00:05:36.460
That sounds good, let's go together.

00:05:45.240 --> 00:05:45.570
If I'm not mistaken, Ms. Yoshinoya's
place is around here.

00:05:45.570 --> 00:05:48.840
Sae
Ryoko Shintani
If I'm not mistaken, Ms. Yoshinoya's
place is around here.

00:05:48.840 --> 00:05:49.670
Yoshinoya

00:05:49.870 --> 00:05:52.080
Since we're here, want to say hello?

00:05:52.080 --> 00:05:53.380
I don't mind.

00:05:53.380 --> 00:05:55.500
Well, then... Ding dong!

00:05:57.980 --> 00:05:58.950
Creeeeak

00:06:01.050 --> 00:06:01.650
Ms. Yoshinoya?

00:06:01.650 --> 00:06:01.920
Relieved
Ms. Yoshinoya?

00:06:01.920 --> 00:06:02.650
Relieved
Oh, it's just you, sorry.

00:06:02.650 --> 00:06:06.160
Oh, it's just you, sorry.

00:06:06.160 --> 00:06:10.190
My younger relatives have been pestering
me for New Year's gifts over the break.

00:06:10.190 --> 00:06:11.890
I was on my guard.

00:06:12.900 --> 00:06:15.830
I'm still young enough to be receiving them.

00:06:15.830 --> 00:06:18.390
How rude of them! Don't you agree?

00:06:21.310 --> 00:06:22.840
Come on in!

00:06:22.840 --> 00:06:24.940
I can't really entertain you though.

00:06:24.940 --> 00:06:26.040
Is that all right?

00:06:26.040 --> 00:06:27.480
I'm coming in!

00:06:27.950 --> 00:06:29.550
I'm coming in!

00:06:29.550 --> 00:06:32.280
Is your family home?

00:06:32.280 --> 00:06:34.420
They're going shopping right now.

00:06:34.420 --> 00:06:36.280
You don't need to worry about them.

00:06:40.890 --> 00:06:42.230
This situation...

00:06:42.230 --> 00:06:46.600
If I were a boy, I would try to hime-hajime.

00:06:46.600 --> 00:06:47.620
[Hime-hajime is the Japanese expression for
the first time a couple has sex in the new year.
It translates roughly as "Princess Initiation."]

00:06:48.070 --> 00:06:49.260
Princess?

00:06:50.270 --> 00:06:51.890
Well, once again...

00:06:52.070 --> 00:06:54.440
Happy New Year.

00:06:54.640 --> 00:06:56.440
Happy New Year!

00:06:56.670 --> 00:06:58.400
Happy New Year.

00:06:58.780 --> 00:07:00.380
I hope to see you around this year.

00:07:00.380 --> 00:07:03.310
Yes, I hope to see you around this year too.

00:07:03.310 --> 00:07:06.080
You all went home, didn't you?

00:07:06.080 --> 00:07:07.890
Did you make your first
shrine visit of the year?

00:07:07.890 --> 00:07:10.190
We still haven't yet.

00:07:10.190 --> 00:07:12.290
We're on our way there right now.

00:07:12.290 --> 00:07:14.780
Care to come with us?

00:07:15.030 --> 00:07:18.100
Oh my! Thank you very much.

00:07:18.100 --> 00:07:19.600
In that case, excuse me for a second.

00:07:19.600 --> 00:07:22.600
Please wait for me while I get changed.

00:07:22.600 --> 00:07:23.300
Okay!

00:07:23.300 --> 00:07:23.600
Thank you for waiting.
Okay!

00:07:23.600 --> 00:07:24.640
Thank you for waiting.

00:07:24.640 --> 00:07:25.800
That was quick!

00:07:26.070 --> 00:07:27.300
Happy New Year.

00:07:29.410 --> 00:07:32.140
It isn't very crowded anymore, is it?

00:07:32.210 --> 00:07:33.840
Yeah...

00:07:33.840 --> 00:07:34.980
That's cold!

00:07:34.980 --> 00:07:37.310
There's a formal way to do this.

00:07:37.310 --> 00:07:38.020
Did you know that?

00:07:38.020 --> 00:07:38.520
Was it right, then left?
Did you know that?

00:07:38.520 --> 00:07:39.980
Was it right, then left?

00:07:40.950 --> 00:07:44.610
Happy New Year, Yokozuna.

00:07:44.920 --> 00:07:46.890
Yokozuna?

00:07:47.730 --> 00:07:49.120
No!

00:07:49.630 --> 00:07:50.290
Jeez!

00:07:50.290 --> 00:07:50.860
Wait, Hiro!
Jeez!

00:07:50.860 --> 00:07:51.700
Wait, Hiro!

00:07:51.700 --> 00:07:55.100
Do all of you know what to do
when you visit a shrine?

00:07:55.230 --> 00:07:56.260
Here I go!

00:08:06.280 --> 00:08:09.210
I mistook a 50 yen coin for a 5 yen coin!

00:08:09.210 --> 00:08:11.110
I'm sure you'll get good luck.

00:08:12.350 --> 00:08:13.320
One prayer Two claps Two prayers

00:08:13.680 --> 00:08:20.660
This is Miyako of Midori City, Asagi-cho
4-16, Hidamari Apartments, Room 202.

00:08:20.660 --> 00:08:22.760
Wh-What are you saying, Miya-chan?

00:08:22.760 --> 00:08:27.600
The gods will have a hard time granting my
wish, if I don't tell them my address.

00:08:27.600 --> 00:08:28.630
Oh?

00:08:28.630 --> 00:08:30.200
She's got to be kidding.

00:08:30.200 --> 00:08:32.600
Now that we're done with our visit,
what should we do next?

00:08:32.600 --> 00:08:34.830
Draw our fortunes, of course.

00:08:35.670 --> 00:08:38.840
I hope my luck this year is
"lucky" or "very lucky."

00:08:38.840 --> 00:08:40.170
I'm looking forward to it.

00:08:40.410 --> 00:08:42.440
Which should I choose?

00:08:44.250 --> 00:08:44.920
Sae...

00:08:44.920 --> 00:08:46.410
I'm getting nervous.

00:08:50.720 --> 00:08:52.390
Super Lucky
You are amazing!

00:08:52.390 --> 00:08:55.190
Super Lucky
You are amazing!
Yuno, take a look at this godly pick.

00:08:55.330 --> 00:08:56.630
That's incredible!

00:08:56.630 --> 00:08:58.000
I got "lucky."

00:08:58.000 --> 00:08:59.060
Let's see...

00:08:59.060 --> 00:09:00.960
"You will receive unexpected help."

00:09:00.960 --> 00:09:04.200
"Surprising things will happen, but if you
don't panic, you'll get your wish."

00:09:04.600 --> 00:09:06.670
I guess it's telling me not to be anxious.

00:09:06.670 --> 00:09:09.440
I'm more curious about the "unexpected help."

00:09:09.440 --> 00:09:10.640
Who could it talking about?

00:09:10.640 --> 00:09:12.040
Wouldn't that be you?

00:09:12.040 --> 00:09:14.450
I'm not unexpected.

00:09:14.450 --> 00:09:16.500
It's probably someone more unlikely.

00:09:16.680 --> 00:09:20.850
For example, the person who
gave you that fan letter.

00:09:20.850 --> 00:09:24.320
I see, that would be unexpected.

00:09:24.320 --> 00:09:25.980
That really made me happy.

00:09:27.220 --> 00:09:29.830
It was my first fan letter.

00:09:29.830 --> 00:09:31.620
I think about it even now.

00:09:31.860 --> 00:09:33.490
I was really happy.

00:09:33.630 --> 00:09:38.100
It let me know that people are
reading the stories I write.

00:09:38.100 --> 00:09:39.300
That's good.

00:09:39.300 --> 00:09:41.030
He was pretty ardent.

00:09:41.470 --> 00:09:45.110
He's been watching you ever
since you made your debut.

00:09:45.110 --> 00:09:46.440
How romantic.

00:09:46.910 --> 00:09:52.950
I feel kind of impressed when I think about
how my message has reached a stranger.

00:09:52.950 --> 00:09:56.890
I really felt like I needed to try my best.

00:09:56.890 --> 00:09:59.220
It helped me a lot.

00:10:04.190 --> 00:10:06.790
Wow, my fortune is "very lucky."

00:10:06.960 --> 00:10:08.100
Nice.

00:10:08.100 --> 00:10:08.700
Let's see...

00:10:08.700 --> 00:10:09.200
Misfortune
Let's see...

00:10:09.200 --> 00:10:09.470
Misfortune

00:10:09.470 --> 00:10:10.670
Number 54
Misfortune
Principal Angered
No Luck With Men
Southern Friends
Autumn

00:10:10.670 --> 00:10:11.630
Fold

00:10:12.140 --> 00:10:15.070
It will be all right if I tie it into
a knot in my mouth, right?

00:10:15.070 --> 00:10:16.310
No!

00:10:16.310 --> 00:10:17.530
I did it!

00:10:18.180 --> 00:10:21.540
Do all of you have your things?

00:10:22.950 --> 00:10:26.180
Please help me to be honest
with my feelings this year!

00:10:26.280 --> 00:10:27.550
Huh? Natsume?

00:10:38.160 --> 00:10:41.360
Hiro's place is the most relaxing.

00:10:41.670 --> 00:10:47.800
As thanks, I wish you a
Happy New Year once again.

00:10:48.110 --> 00:10:49.940
Miya-chan, how many times
have you said that?

00:10:50.240 --> 00:10:54.510
New Year's greetings sound great no
matter how many times I hear them.

00:10:54.510 --> 00:10:57.020
They have a festive feeling to them.

00:10:57.020 --> 00:11:00.520
Then once more! Happy New Year!

00:11:00.520 --> 00:11:01.850
That's enough!

00:11:02.960 --> 00:11:07.190
Come to think of it, you stayed here
until the year was almost over.

00:11:07.390 --> 00:11:11.030
Yeah, I ended up going home on the 30th.

00:11:11.030 --> 00:11:14.070
It was rough since the bullet train was packed!

00:11:14.070 --> 00:11:18.370
I already had a ticket,
so I went home on the 26th.

00:11:18.370 --> 00:11:21.510
But I was worried about you
for three days after that.

00:11:21.510 --> 00:11:22.980
Oh, sorry.

00:11:22.980 --> 00:11:25.670
I can't remember what I ate.

00:11:26.110 --> 00:11:29.670
Even though I went home, Chika had cram
school until the end of the year.

00:11:30.050 --> 00:11:32.320
For me, the New Year started on the 2nd,

00:11:32.320 --> 00:11:34.010
so I wasn't really in the mood
to celebrate the new year.

00:11:34.250 --> 00:11:37.590
The time before entrance exams
is most important.

00:11:37.590 --> 00:11:41.890
Yeah, she may not act it,
but she seemed oddly tense.

00:11:42.160 --> 00:11:46.720
When I try not to say anything that will
offend her, I end up doing it anyway.

00:11:48.130 --> 00:11:50.070
Slip! Fall! Sink!

00:11:50.070 --> 00:11:51.500
Miya-chan!

00:11:51.500 --> 00:11:53.010
I'm sorry!

00:11:53.010 --> 00:11:56.940
She gets angry at every little thing.

00:11:56.940 --> 00:11:59.880
When I see her, I can't resist teasing her!

00:11:59.880 --> 00:12:01.350
That sounds tough.

00:12:01.350 --> 00:12:02.380
Yeah...

00:12:02.380 --> 00:12:05.350
Even though everyone thinks that
asking her if she's all right

00:12:05.350 --> 00:12:07.190
or telling her to try her best
puts pressure on her,

00:12:07.190 --> 00:12:09.180
everyone ends up saying it anyway.

00:12:09.920 --> 00:12:12.360
What did all of you do for New Year's?

00:12:12.360 --> 00:12:15.130
I was always eating something.

00:12:15.130 --> 00:12:16.650
That sounds like you.

00:12:16.960 --> 00:12:22.940
Sea bream, flounder, tuna, crab, shrimp,
teriyaki yellowtail, osechi and ozoni.

00:12:22.940 --> 00:12:25.060
That sounds like Ryugu Palace.

00:12:25.310 --> 00:12:28.980
My family only goes all out
for occasions like this.

00:12:28.980 --> 00:12:30.880
I really stuffed myself.

00:12:30.880 --> 00:12:34.250
I'm jealous that you don't have
to worry about your weight.

00:12:34.250 --> 00:12:37.680
You should have wished to have that
solved when we visited the shrine.

00:12:37.850 --> 00:12:39.320
Well...

00:12:39.620 --> 00:12:41.650
What did all of you wish for?

00:12:41.650 --> 00:12:45.350
I wanted to be able to have my fill
of rice for the whole year.

00:12:45.490 --> 00:12:47.480
I... Umm...

00:12:47.990 --> 00:12:53.490
I wanted everyone to remain healthy and
I wanted to become better at drawing.

00:12:56.670 --> 00:12:58.500
That sounds like you.

00:12:58.500 --> 00:13:00.770
Miya-chan's also sounds typical.

00:13:00.770 --> 00:13:04.140
What did you two wish for?

00:13:04.140 --> 00:13:05.950
Mine was about work.

00:13:05.950 --> 00:13:07.550
I...

00:13:07.550 --> 00:13:09.420
I really can't say!

00:13:09.420 --> 00:13:11.220
Huh? What's wrong?

00:13:11.220 --> 00:13:12.750
Is it that serious?

00:13:12.750 --> 00:13:14.950
No, that's not it.

00:13:17.020 --> 00:13:20.530
Tell us, Hiro, it will make you feel better.

00:13:20.530 --> 00:13:23.000
Umm, you don't have to tell us.

00:13:23.000 --> 00:13:25.760
It's exactly what you're thinking.

00:13:25.970 --> 00:13:29.200
I wished to be able to diet
successfully this year.

00:13:29.600 --> 00:13:33.830
Come to think of it, I wished the
same thing last year.

00:13:34.170 --> 00:13:36.810
I'm embarrassed thinking about it.

00:13:36.810 --> 00:13:38.910
Is that all?

00:13:38.910 --> 00:13:40.950
There's no need to talk about it like that.

00:13:40.950 --> 00:13:42.780
I was serious.

00:13:43.920 --> 00:13:46.090
My willpower is just weak.

00:13:46.090 --> 00:13:47.950
That's not true.

00:13:47.950 --> 00:13:53.450
I'm sure the gods felt that you
didn't need to go on a diet.

00:13:54.190 --> 00:13:57.000
Thank you, Yuno, I'll try my best.

00:13:57.000 --> 00:13:58.160
O-Okay!

00:13:59.370 --> 00:14:03.370
On a side note, what do you suppose
Ms. Yoshinoya wished for?

00:14:03.370 --> 00:14:06.100
She's really unpredictable.

00:14:06.470 --> 00:14:09.840
"I wish to be spared the
principal's anger this year."

00:14:09.840 --> 00:14:12.900
"First, you need to repent your actions."

00:14:14.210 --> 00:14:16.080
Natsume also came.

00:14:16.450 --> 00:14:18.380
She left in a hurry though.

00:14:19.290 --> 00:14:22.250
I just don't understand her.

00:14:23.190 --> 00:14:26.160
Natsume! Happy New Year!

00:14:26.160 --> 00:14:28.030
Are you making your first shrine
visit of the year only now?

00:14:28.030 --> 00:14:29.630
O-Oh, Happy New Year.

00:14:29.630 --> 00:14:31.600
I just came with someone else.

00:14:31.900 --> 00:14:33.070
Why have you come this late?

00:14:33.070 --> 00:14:36.560
Was there something you wanted to wish for?

00:14:37.040 --> 00:14:38.340
Wish?

00:14:38.340 --> 00:14:41.570
Well, we ended up coming with Yosshi.

00:14:41.570 --> 00:14:42.670
Yosshi?

00:14:43.140 --> 00:14:44.310
Oh...

00:14:44.310 --> 00:14:48.010
By the way, what were you
wishing so fervently for?

00:14:48.150 --> 00:14:52.250
Nothing special, things related to
work and my sister.

00:14:52.250 --> 00:14:53.020
What about you?

00:14:53.020 --> 00:14:54.080
Me?

00:14:54.720 --> 00:14:55.820
I...

00:14:55.820 --> 00:14:59.310
I wished for world peace and the
prosperity of the human race!

00:15:00.960 --> 00:15:06.060
That's pretty grand. I never knew you
thought about things like that.

00:15:06.770 --> 00:15:08.670
I hope you get your wish.

00:15:08.670 --> 00:15:09.500
Huh?

00:15:09.500 --> 00:15:13.200
I said, I hope you get your wish.

00:15:14.940 --> 00:15:17.600
N-No, you've got the wrong idea.

00:15:17.980 --> 00:15:19.040
See you later!

00:15:23.280 --> 00:15:26.310
Thank you, I hope to see you around this year.

00:15:29.390 --> 00:15:30.820
I hope to see you around.

00:15:31.890 --> 00:15:34.380
Natsume was acting kind of strange today.

00:15:34.960 --> 00:15:39.130
What sort of relationship does Natsume
Sempai have with you, Sae?

00:15:39.130 --> 00:15:44.760
She seemed hostile to you on field day,
but I think she wants to be your friend.

00:15:45.910 --> 00:15:47.170
What do you think, Hiro?

00:15:47.170 --> 00:15:49.910
Huh? Me? Well, why not?

00:15:49.910 --> 00:15:51.280
Yeah...

00:15:51.280 --> 00:15:53.110
Yeah... And?

00:15:53.110 --> 00:15:54.450
And?

00:15:54.450 --> 00:15:57.110
I don't hate her.

00:15:58.180 --> 00:16:00.490
Me neither.

00:16:00.490 --> 00:16:03.690
I think I ate too many tangerines
over winter break.

00:16:03.690 --> 00:16:07.390
Me too. You just can't help it
when they're placed out.

00:16:07.630 --> 00:16:10.720
You complain that there are only tangerines
in the house, but still eat them.

00:16:11.200 --> 00:16:14.790
We got a lot of them every day
from the landlady.

00:16:15.030 --> 00:16:17.260
We sure met a lot of people today.

00:16:17.770 --> 00:16:21.740
I think this is the first time I've ever
seen the landlady so happy.

00:16:21.740 --> 00:16:24.210
I couldn't tell who she was at first!

00:16:24.210 --> 00:16:25.180
Yeah!

00:16:26.180 --> 00:16:29.640
Sorry, I absolutely must get this milk.

00:16:35.520 --> 00:16:37.620
Huh? Is that the landlady?

00:16:37.620 --> 00:16:38.290
What?!

00:16:38.290 --> 00:16:38.790
She's wearing a kimono!
What?!

00:16:38.790 --> 00:16:39.760
She's wearing a kimono!

00:16:41.390 --> 00:16:43.300
Hey! Long time no see!

00:16:43.300 --> 00:16:45.420
Happy New Year.

00:16:45.770 --> 00:16:47.390
Happy New Year.

00:16:47.700 --> 00:16:50.030
Happy New Year. I see you're back already.

00:16:50.100 --> 00:16:52.510
Yes, we start school tomorrow.

00:16:52.510 --> 00:16:54.840
That's good.

00:16:57.280 --> 00:17:01.210
This? I don't usually dress up like this.

00:17:01.210 --> 00:17:02.680
Does it look strange?

00:17:03.820 --> 00:17:05.380
It's very wonderful.

00:17:05.380 --> 00:17:06.950
Yeah!

00:17:06.950 --> 00:17:11.090
All right, I'm going to give you a reward!

00:17:11.090 --> 00:17:13.390
Wow, Ehime tangerines.

00:17:13.390 --> 00:17:16.560
I wish you a happy New Year.

00:17:17.960 --> 00:17:20.270
I was invited to a New Year's party today.

00:17:20.270 --> 00:17:21.570
I got that as a gift.

00:17:21.570 --> 00:17:24.000
And now, I'm going to another New Year's party.

00:17:26.140 --> 00:17:28.940
Take care and study hard!

00:17:28.940 --> 00:17:32.640
If you do, you'll have a lot of fun
when you're an adult!

00:17:32.950 --> 00:17:33.810
See you later!

00:17:33.810 --> 00:17:35.110
She seems so happy.

00:17:35.110 --> 00:17:37.170
She seems to be in high spirits.

00:17:39.090 --> 00:17:40.750
Miya-chan, want to take these?

00:17:40.750 --> 00:17:44.020
I'm grateful, but I have boxes of them at home.

00:17:44.390 --> 00:17:46.050
I'm from a tangerine-producing
region after all.

00:17:46.330 --> 00:17:47.990
Well, I'm going to put them away.

00:17:47.990 --> 00:17:48.960
Growl...

00:17:49.900 --> 00:17:51.700
Care to have dinner?

00:17:51.700 --> 00:17:53.600
Or would you like some ozoni?

00:17:53.600 --> 00:17:54.470
Dinner!

00:17:54.470 --> 00:17:57.230
I have mentaiko, so I think dinner is good.

00:17:57.800 --> 00:17:58.900
U-Umm...

00:17:59.310 --> 00:18:01.360
Care to eat in my room?

00:18:01.740 --> 00:18:04.110
I have souvenirs for all of you.

00:18:05.080 --> 00:18:07.570
All right, let's go to Yunocchi's room!

00:18:10.080 --> 00:18:11.420
Whoa...

00:18:11.420 --> 00:18:13.350
It looks like a produce fair.

00:18:13.890 --> 00:18:18.320
Mentaiko, pumpkin, sandfish and
pickled vegetables from all over.

00:18:18.590 --> 00:18:22.030
I thought that I should display
all of your souvenirs.

00:18:22.030 --> 00:18:23.830
This is pretty fun.

00:18:24.230 --> 00:18:27.130
Ozoni differs from region
to region, doesn't it?

00:18:27.430 --> 00:18:30.340
The one we make at my place uses a
clear broth and has chicken in it.

00:18:30.340 --> 00:18:32.170
It's probably similar to the ones in Tokyo.

00:18:32.740 --> 00:18:35.410
The one we make at my place
is soy sauce flavored

00:18:35.410 --> 00:18:37.440
and has vegetables and burdock root in it.

00:18:37.440 --> 00:18:38.640
It's delicious.

00:18:38.840 --> 00:18:40.380
The one we make at my place

00:18:40.380 --> 00:18:43.880
uses a clear broth and has chicken,
ginko nuts and fish cakes in it.

00:18:43.880 --> 00:18:47.220
The one we make at my place
is soy sauce flavored

00:18:47.220 --> 00:18:49.120
and has various vegetables
and white meat in it.

00:18:49.120 --> 00:18:52.280
I felt really relieved to eat it at home.

00:18:52.730 --> 00:18:54.990
It tastes like home cooking.

00:18:55.390 --> 00:19:00.900
Your parents didn't really
want to let you leave.

00:19:00.900 --> 00:19:03.230
Did they make a lot of good food for you?

00:19:03.300 --> 00:19:08.470
Yeah, I told them they didn't have to,
but they kept getting me to try things.

00:19:08.470 --> 00:19:12.210
Yeah, they do it even though you
tell them you're stuffed.

00:19:12.650 --> 00:19:14.200
Still, it's nice.

00:19:14.910 --> 00:19:15.970
Yeah!

00:19:18.220 --> 00:19:21.240
I really feel like I'm back at
Hidamari Apartments.

00:19:21.620 --> 00:19:23.950
We're starting school tomorrow, huh?

00:19:24.320 --> 00:19:26.090
What do all of you plan to do this semester?

00:19:27.890 --> 00:19:29.360
The same as usual, I suppose.

00:19:29.730 --> 00:19:32.200
Try to be successful in my work and studies.

00:19:32.400 --> 00:19:33.630
What about you, Yuno?

00:19:33.700 --> 00:19:39.270
I want to study art more and
expand my expertise.

00:19:39.270 --> 00:19:41.140
I want to build up my stamina!

00:19:41.610 --> 00:19:44.980
I want to develop a strong mind and
body that won't give in to anything!

00:19:44.980 --> 00:19:47.910
Miyako, you don't have to
work on that anymore.

00:19:47.910 --> 00:19:48.950
What about you, Hiro?

00:19:48.950 --> 00:19:53.680
Well, I suppose I want to work harder
to become my ideal self.

00:19:54.020 --> 00:19:57.060
Both of you sure are amazing!

00:19:57.060 --> 00:20:00.250
Not really, we're still working at it.

00:20:00.590 --> 00:20:03.860
Hiro, how many more kilos until
you reach your perfect self?

00:20:04.260 --> 00:20:05.890
Jeez!

00:20:09.140 --> 00:20:11.900
I should get going.
I have to prepare for tomorrow.

00:20:11.900 --> 00:20:16.930
Well, everyone, have a good year...
I mean, have a goodnight!

00:20:17.710 --> 00:20:18.740
See you later!

00:20:18.740 --> 00:20:20.010
Goodnight!

00:20:20.010 --> 00:20:21.100
See you!

00:20:37.160 --> 00:20:38.300
What is it?

00:20:38.300 --> 00:20:39.230
What's wrong?

00:20:39.230 --> 00:20:40.260
Yuno?

00:20:45.740 --> 00:20:47.210
I'm back.

00:20:53.780 --> 00:20:55.510
Welcome home.

00:21:06.490 --> 00:21:09.760
Hidamari Apartments really is wonderful.

00:21:09.830 --> 00:21:10.330
Hi

00:21:10.330 --> 00:21:10.830
da

00:21:10.830 --> 00:21:11.330
ma

00:21:11.330 --> 00:21:11.830
ri

00:21:11.830 --> 00:21:12.760
Apartments

00:21:12.900 --> 00:21:19.870
What color do I feel like now?

00:21:19.870 --> 00:21:23.140
Smile white? Tear blue?

00:21:23.140 --> 00:21:26.350
I try overlapping them

00:21:26.350 --> 00:21:30.750
Today is sunny!

00:21:30.750 --> 00:21:36.360
On the canvas, I'm having iced
milk and drinking ramune!

00:21:36.360 --> 00:21:39.720
I've got vibrant color toppings

00:21:39.960 --> 00:21:41.480
Wahaha!

00:21:41.990 --> 00:21:49.420
It's not like that, that's just fine

00:21:50.040 --> 00:21:55.340
We'll have fruits as our model

00:21:55.710 --> 00:22:01.950
Come on, let's draw

00:22:01.950 --> 00:22:05.180
It's our homework!

00:22:07.650 --> 00:22:09.620
January 10 The End

00:22:19.100 --> 00:22:25.400
An unknown world stretched out

00:22:25.400 --> 00:22:31.140
Connecting, endless connecting threads

00:22:31.780 --> 00:22:38.180
An upside down world is pretty fun

00:22:38.180 --> 00:22:43.990
Connecting, never-ending threads

00:22:44.360 --> 00:22:50.060
You are smiling somewhere today

00:22:50.600 --> 00:22:55.630
I will run all night until the day we meet again

00:22:55.630 --> 00:22:57.240
Run all night

00:22:57.240 --> 00:23:00.310
The record of a resounding shooting star

00:23:00.310 --> 00:23:03.640
Your singing voice

00:23:03.640 --> 00:23:06.710
Touches my heart

00:23:06.710 --> 00:23:09.980
A sky full of shooting stars

00:23:09.980 --> 00:23:13.120
The record of a shining shooting star

00:23:13.120 --> 00:23:16.320
Your whispering voice

00:23:16.320 --> 00:23:19.760
Leads me through space

00:23:19.760 --> 00:23:22.630
A song about shooting stars

00:23:22.630 --> 00:23:26.170
I can't hear them

00:23:26.170 --> 00:23:30.100
I can't reach them

00:23:30.100 --> 00:23:34.660
The footsteps I'm looking for

00:23:42.700 --> 00:23:44.670
Preview
I have a question on Yunocchi's behalf.

00:23:44.670 --> 00:23:46.980
Preview
What's the best way to make use of a holiday?

00:23:46.980 --> 00:23:48.410
Preview
Why is it on her behalf?

00:23:48.410 --> 00:23:51.010
Preview
Miya-chan, I never told you to ask that!

00:23:51.010 --> 00:23:52.710
Preview
Probably study, right?

00:23:52.710 --> 00:23:53.980
Preview
Do work.

00:23:53.980 --> 00:23:57.790
Preview
Wake up at six, go jogging, clean my room,
study at the library,

00:23:57.790 --> 00:23:59.350
Preview
go home and review for the next day!

00:23:59.350 --> 00:24:00.360
Preview
Do you really do that?!

00:24:00.360 --> 00:24:02.660
Preview
It would be nice if I did.

00:24:02.660 --> 00:24:06.790
Preview
The next episode is "February 24, Polaroidon"

00:24:06.790 --> 00:24:08.430
Preview
We'll be waiting at Hidamari Apartments.

00:24:08.430 --> 00:24:10.430
Preview
Be sure to tune in!

00:24:10.430 --> 00:24:11.730
Preview
